title: Display modes
tags: GUI
kind: reference
aliases: display-mode mode grid table
summary: A panel that can lay out the same content in several ways — metarecord-list as a table or a grid — keeps its mode per workspace.

A ''display mode'' is one of several layouts a panel type offers for the same
content. It is part of the panel's state in its workspace: another workspace's list
keeps its own mode, and the mode survives switching the slot to another panel type
and back — not the end of the session.

[[metarecord-list panel]] has two:

* `table` (the default) — one row per metarecord, one column per chosen field;
* `grid` — a thumbnail per metarecord, for image and video collections.

`metarecord-list:set mode grid` and `metarecord-list:set mode table` switch between
them.

Other panels choose their layout from what they show rather than offering a mode:
the `file` panel previews a file, and shows a folder as a grid of thumbnails.
